<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Understanding Polynomials</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01569</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Understanding Polynomials</md:title>
    <md:uuid>162749c6-a826-413a-acb5-51e99ff2a816</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Activity</title>
<para id="para-00002">A <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00001">monomial</term> is an algebraic expression with exactly one term: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
<para id="para-00003">A <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00002">binomial</term> is an algebraic expression with exactly two terms: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
<para id="para-00004">A <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00003">trinomial</term> is an algebraic expression with exactly three terms: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
<para id="para-00005">Monomials, binomials, and trinomials are all different types of polynomials. A <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00004">polynomial</term> is a monomial or two or more monomials combined by addition or subtraction.</para>
<para id="para-00006">The <term class="glossary-tooltip" id="term-00005">degree of a polynomial</term> is the highest degree of all its terms.</para>

<note id="note-00001" class="link-to-learning">
    <para id="para-00007">Log into <link url="https://student.desmos.com">student.desmos.com</link> using the information provided by your teacher to complete the activity.</para>
  </note>

  <para id="para-00001">Examine the following expressions and use them to answer questions 1 – 6.</para>
  <table class="unnumbered" id="table-00001">
    <tgroup cols="1">
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry align="center"><m:math display="inline"><m:msup>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
          </m:msup></m:math></entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
          </m:mrow></m:math></entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mn>8</m:mn>
            <m:msup>
            <m:mi>d</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            <m:mi>e</m:mi>
            <m:mo>-</m:mo>
            <m:mi>g</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center">
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mi>h</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center">
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mn>15</m:mn>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry align="center">
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
         <row>
          <entry align="center">
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>z</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
          </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </tgroup>
  </table>

  <exercise id="exer-00001">
    <problem id="prob-00001">
      <para id="para-00008">1. Which of the polynomials listed above are monomials?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00001">
      <para id="para-00009">There are four answers: <m:math display="inline"><m:msup>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
          </m:msup></m:math>,
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mn>15</m:mn>
            </m:mrow></m:math>,
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>z</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>,
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
        </para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>

  <exercise id="exer-00002">
    <problem id="prob-00002">
      <para id="para-00010">2. Which of the polynomials listed above are binomials?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00002">
      <para id="para-00011">There are two answers:
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
          </m:mrow></m:math>,
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mi>h</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
      </para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>

  <exercise id="exer-00003">
    <problem id="prob-00003">
      <para id="para-00012">3. Which of the polynomials listed above are trinomials?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00003">
      <para id="para-00013">There are two answers:
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mn>8</m:mn>
            <m:msup>
            <m:mi>d</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            <m:mi>e</m:mi>
            <m:mo>-</m:mo>
            <m:mi>g</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>,
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
      </para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>

  <exercise id="exer-00004">
    <problem id="prob-00004">
      <para id="para-00014">4. Which of the polynomials listed above have a degree of 0?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00004">
      <para id="para-00015">There is only one answer: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mn>15</m:mn>
            </m:mrow></m:math></para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>

  <exercise id="exer-00005">
    <problem id="prob-00005">
      <para id="para-00016">5. Which of the polynomials listed above have a degree of 1?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00005">
      <para id="para-00017">There are three answers:
        <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
          </m:mrow></m:math>,
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mi>h</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>,
             <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:mi>z</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>
      </para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>

  <exercise id="exer-00006">
    <problem id="prob-00006">
      <para id="para-00018">6. Which of the polynomials listed above have a degree of 2?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution id="sol-00006">
      <para id="para-00019">There are four answers: 
        <m:math display="inline"><m:msup>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
          </m:msup></m:math>,
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mn>8</m:mn>
            <m:msup>
            <m:mi>d</m:mi>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            </m:msup>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>3</m:mn>
            <m:mi>e</m:mi>
            <m:mo>-</m:mo>
            <m:mi>g</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>,
            <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>-</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow></m:math>, and 
<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow>
            <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            <m:mi>n</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
      </para>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
</section>
</content>
</document>